<title>BELGIUM: EU says CL rescue money is to maintain status quo.</title>
<headline>EU says CL rescue money is to maintain status quo.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Competition Commissioner Karel Van Miert said on Wednesday that the 3.9 billion French francs the Commission had approved in emergency aid for Credit Lyonnais was designed to maintain the status quo at the bank until the end of the year.</p>
<p>&quot;This money is to maintain the status quo until the end of the year....It's a kind of measure to freeze the situation. Not to let it deteriorate,&quot; he told a news conference.  </p>
<p>He also said the money would be considered in the Commission's new probe into a further bailout plan for the bank.</p>
<p>&quot;The amount of money obviously has to be taken into account when we talk about counter measures,&quot; he said.</p>
</text>
